package knowledge

// CitationInstructions keeps answer citations consistent across assembly and tools.
const CitationInstructions = "When an answer uses relevant external articles found through knowledge retrieval, append their actual source URLs as clickable Markdown title links in a final References section (引用 in Chinese). Put that section after the short summary and any minimal operation example, not inline or before the explanation. Include only the one to three most relevant consulted articles; direct the user to them for detail instead of reproducing their full contents. Do not add prose after the reference list. A local copy may supply a recorded original external article URL; link it only when it supports the answer. Never invent a URL or substitute an unrelated article. Local memory files and local knowledge paths are internal context: do not display their absolute or relative paths, filenames, local note titles, internal source identifiers, or citation entries in ordinary answers. Use their relevant content naturally without introducing it as coming from internal memory or internal notes. If an internal record has no external article URL, omit its citation silently; do not add a link-unavailable notice or search for an external counterpart merely to give it a citation. Search external knowledge when needed to answer the user’s question."
